/-!
# The actual elliptic patch comparison for the prescribed canonical line

The prescribed Cartier line maps fibrewise complex-linearly and
holomorphically to the original canonical bundle on the entire order-four
elliptic patch.  Its literal preferred-unit multiplier supplies the
transition-data interface for the global gluing.  The actual Cartier
section maps to the genuine elliptic extension, including its central
zeros, and hence to the regular canonical form on the punctured overlap.
All structures and local coefficient identities use the original bundle
atlases; no global comparison is assumed here.
-/
